# Frontend Trivy ignore — PAT-157
# -------------------------------
# axios 1.15.0 has 4 HIGH CVEs flagged by Trivy:
#   - CVE-2026-42033: HTTP Transport Hijacking via Prototype (fixed in 1.15.1)
#   - CVE-2026-42035: Arbitrary HTTP header injection via prototype (fixed in 1.15.1)
#   - CVE-2026-42043: NO_PROXY bypass via crafted URL (fixed in 1.15.1)
#   - CVE-2026-42264: (fixed in 1.15.2)
#
# Status (2026-05-09): axios 1.15.1 / 1.15.2 are NOT yet published to the npm
# registry — `npm view axios@1.15.1` returns 404. Trivy's vulnerability DB lists
# them as fixed but upstream has not shipped them yet. We are pinned to 1.15.0
# until the patched releases land.
#
# Exposure assessment (VEX):
# - CVE-2026-42033 / -42035 (prototype-based hijacking / header injection):
#   only exploitable when application code passes attacker-controlled input
#   through `Object.prototype` mutation. Our `api/client.ts` uses a pre-built
#   axios instance with hard-coded interceptors and never accepts user-controlled
#   prototype mutations. Risk: LOW.
# - CVE-2026-42043 (NO_PROXY bypass): NO_PROXY env var is not set in our deploys
#   (frontend is a static SPA bundle; axios runs only inside the user's browser,
#   not behind a corporate proxy). Risk: NEGLIGIBLE.
# - CVE-2026-42264: requires axios 1.15.2; details limited; same SPA-only
#   exposure profile. Risk: LOW.
#
# Tracked: bump axios as soon as 1.15.1+ is published to npm.
CVE-2026-42033
CVE-2026-42035
CVE-2026-42043
CVE-2026-42264
